<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZILIAN RESULTS/STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of weekend</p>
<p>matches in the Sao Paulo and Rio de Janeiro soccer</p>
<p>championships.</p>
<p>Sao Paulo championship</p>
<p> Aracatuba		  3    Guarani			0	</p>
<p>Corinthians		1    Botafogo-Ribeirao Preto  0</p>
<p> Internacional Limeira  0    Sao Jose		     1</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		 0    Santos			 2</p>
<p> Palmeiras		  2    Sao Paulo		    4</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista    1    Portuguesa		   2</p>
<p> Rio Branco		 2    Juventus		     1</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	   3    America/S.J.Rio Preto    5</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against points)</p>
<p>Group One</p>
<p> Palmeiras		 20 12  6  2 51 24 42</p>
<p> Portuguesa		20 11  6  3 42 26 39</p>
<p> Santos		    20 10  7  3 37 23 37</p>
<p> Guarani		   20  5  8  7 34 44 23</p>
<p> Sao Jose		  20  4  7  9 25 35 19</p>
<p> Juventus		  20  3  6 11 33 50 15</p>
<p> Botafogo		  20  2  8 10 14 27 14</p>
<p> America		   20  3  4 13 21 55 13</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> Corinthians	     20 12  5  3 47 23 41</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		 20  9  9  2 44 22 36</p>
<p> Uniao Sao Joao	  20  7  6  7 28 27 27</p>
<p> Rio Branco		20  7  6  7 27 28 27</p>
<p> Aracatuba		 20  7  5  8 25 26 26</p>
<p>Internacional Limeira 20  6  7  7 33 34 25</p>
<p> Mogi Mirim		20  5  7  8 25 32 22</p>
<p> Portuguesa Santista   20  5  5 10 26 36 20</p>
<p>Note: The teams play once against the other teams in their</p>
<p>own group, then twice against the teams in the other group. At</p>
<p>the end of this, the top two teams in each group qualify for</p>
<p>the final play-off stage. If teams are level on points,</p>
<p>positions are decided by the number of games won.   </p>
<p>Corinthians and Sao Paulo already qualified.</p>
<p>Rio de Janeiro championship, second stage</p>
<p> Americano		  1    Volta Redonda		1</p>
<p> Bangu			0    Maduereira		   0</p>
<p> Flamengo		   2    Vasco da Gama		1</p>
<p> Fluminense		 0    Botafogo		     0</p>
<p>Second stage, final standings</p>
<p> Botafogo		   7  4  3  0  8  4 15</p>
<p> Fluminense		 7  4  3  1 10  5 14</p>
<p> Flamengo		   7  4  2  1 16  9 14</p>
<p> Vasco da Gama	    7  3  1  3  6  6 10</p>
<p> Americano		  7  2  2  3  8 11  8</p>
<p> Bangu			7  1  3  3  6  8  6</p>
<p> Madureira		  7  0  4  3  7 11  4</p>
<p> Volta Redonda	    7  1  1  5  7 14  3</p>
<p>Botafogo win the second stage. Madureira and Volta Redonda</p>
<p>elimininated.</p>
<p>Note: the winners of the first, second and third stages</p>
<p>qualify for the final round. Only the top eight in the first</p>
<p>stage go into the second stage and the top six teams in the</p>
<p>second stage carry on into the third stage. If the same team</p>
<p>wins all three stages, they become champions automatically.</p>
<p>First stage winners - Botafogo</p>
<p>Eliminated in the first stage - Itaperuna, America,</p>
<p>Olaria, Barreira.</p>
